{
  "title": "{ip:Dipende} da te: non rinunciare a insistere",
  "translation": "It's up to you: don't give up insisting",
  "topics": "Choosing prepositions, verbs and adjectives with fixed constructions",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Learn the verb together with its preposition"
      },
      "The preposition often can't be deduced by logic, so a verb and its preposition should be treated as one item. Grouping them by preposition makes them easier to remember.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Preposition",
            "Verbs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a",
              "contribuire a, rinunciare a, tendere a, abituarsi a, riferirsi a, servire a"
            ],
            [
              "di",
              "accorgersi di, occuparsi di, fidarsi di, trattarsi di, vergognarsi di, dubitare di"
            ],
            [
              "da",
              "dipendere da, derivare da, provenire da, astenersi da, guardarsi da"
            ],
            [
              "su",
              "insistere su, basarsi su, contare su, riflettere su, soffermarsi su"
            ],
            [
              "in",
              "consistere in, credere in, specializzarsi in, sfociare in"
            ],
            [
              "con",
              "confrontarsi con, scontrarsi con, congratularsi con"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Before an infinitive"
      },
      "A verb also decides how an infinitive is linked to it.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Link",
            "Verbs",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a",
              "cominciare, riuscire, convincere, costringere, continuare",
              "L'{pp:ho convinto} a restare."
            ],
            [
              "di",
              "decidere, smettere, finire, rischiare, cercare, permettere",
              "{pp:Ha smesso} di fumare."
            ],
            [
              "nothing",
              "potere, volere, dovere, sapere, preferire, bisognare",
              "{ip:Preferisco} restare."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "One verb, two prepositions, two meanings"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Verb",
            "First meaning",
            "Second meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pensare",
              "pensare a: have in mind",
              "pensare di: have an opinion, or to intend"
            ],
            [
              "credere",
              "credere a: believe what's said",
              "credere in: have faith in"
            ],
            [
              "finire",
              "finire di: stop doing",
              "finire per: end up doing"
            ],
            [
              "decidere",
              "decidere di: choose to",
              "decidersi a: make up one's mind"
            ],
            [
              "tenere",
              "tenere a: care about",
              "tenere per: support (a team)"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Adjectives and nouns"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Preposition",
            "Examples"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a",
              "incline a, disposto a, adatto a, contrario a, attento a"
            ],
            [
              "di",
              "capace di, degno di, ricco di, privo di, consapevole di"
            ],
            [
              "in",
              "esperto in, fiducia in"
            ],
            [
              "per",
              "interesse per, rispetto per, passione per"
            ],
            [
              "verso",
              "gentile verso, atteggiamento verso"
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
